<title>USA: Paravant Computer Q2 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Paravant Computer Q2 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE, Fla. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended	 Six Months Ended</p>
<p>			    March 31,		   March 31,</p>
<p>			    1997	1996	  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Revenues	 $3,196,218   $959,608  $5,127,310  $1,724,882</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>			 232,908  (277,837)     125,349   (648,176)</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>number of shares</p>
<p>  outstanding   12,832,984  4,500,000  12,832,984   4,500,000</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per</p>
<p>  share		    .02	(.06)	   .01	 (.14)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said increased revenues, reduced selling and administrative expenses as a percentage of sales, and lower interest expense enabled it to achieve a profit for the current quarter and year-to-date.</p>
<p>The company said per share calculations for all periods give effect to the initial public offering of 1,150,000 common shares and 1,610,000 redeemable warrants on June 3, 1996.</p>
<p>The company said it completed a three-for-one common-stock split on July 25, 1996.  Full name is Paravant Computer Systems Inc.</p>
